@packages/core import { SigilContextRetrieval }
@packages/compiler/src/profile.sigil import { SigilCompilationProfile }

component SigilAgentAdapter {
  goal {
    Map one provider-neutral bounded evaluation request to an enforceable
    code-agent execution without changing compiler semantics.

    Enforce the capability contract from CompilationProfile and emit only evidence
    accepted as CompilationDiagnostic input.
  }

  interface {
    AgentAdapter {
      evaluate(request) returns one completed provider-neutral result containing
      candidate findings, command traces, and model usage containing nonnegative
      integer inputTokens and outputTokens, or rejects without a partial result

      request contains one target, evaluation skill, output schema, snapshot-bound
      immutable read-only workspaceAccess, complete immutable PurposeRetrievalResult,
      AgentCapabilityContract, maxInputChars character limit, execution budgets, and
      cancellation signal

      request also contains non-empty stage, a non-empty ordered allowedRules array
      of unique non-empty rule identifiers, and implementationEvidence equal to
      context-only or compare; none of these fields is nullable

      stage and allowedRules membership is validated by the caller against the
      effective profile and selected evaluation skill; the adapter validates their
      shape but does not redefine either support set

      an absent, null, or empty stage; an absent, null, empty, or duplicate rule; or
      implementationEvidence other than context-only or compare rejects during
      preflight with AGENT_REQUEST_INVALID before prompt rendering or provider
      invocation

      after request-shape validation, every prompt-bound value is validated as
      canonicalizable before capability and budget validation. Admissible values are
      null, booleans, finite JSON numbers, well-formed Unicode strings, arrays of
      admissible values, and string-keyed objects whose defined properties contain
      admissible values; undefined object properties are absent

      an unsupported value, non-finite number, or unpaired Unicode surrogate rejects
      with AGENT_REQUEST_INVALID before capability or budget validation, prompt
      rendering, or provider invocation

      target component, workspaceAccess snapshot fingerprint, and evaluation-stage
      purpose must exactly equal their PurposeRetrievalResult identities; the adapter
      validates this invariant during preflight and rejects a mismatch with
      AGENT_REQUEST_INVALID before provider invocation

      provider cwd is derived only from workspaceAccess.agentRoot; no independently
      supplied root path may select a different mutable or differently fingerprinted
      workspace view

      maxInputChars, elapsedTimeMs, maxCommands, maxCommandOutputChars,
      maxInputTokens, and maxOutputTokens are positive safe integers; zero, negative,
      fractional, non-finite, nonnumeric, and unsafe-integer values reject during
      preflight with AGENT_BUDGET_INVALID and perform no provider invocation

      evaluate receives only provider-neutral evaluation inputs; the adapter instance
      already carries its optional bound model

      AgentCapabilityContract is supplied by SigilCompilationProfile. Its preventive
      constraints must be enforceable without broadening, while allowedCommands is
      enforced as the exact operation-settlement policy defined by that contract

      returned events have valid provider framing and a structurally valid final
      findings object; candidate findings remain untrusted until compiler rule,
      evidence, semantic-subject, and diagnostic validation succeeds

      provider-specific cached, reasoning, or other usage measures may be absent, but
      inputTokens and outputTokens are mandatory for every successful result

      result contains configuredModel as the bound model or null and resolvedModel as
      the provider-reported executed model or null when the provider does not report
      it; resolvedModel never substitutes for configuredModel

      when configuredModel and resolvedModel are both non-null they must be exactly
      equal opaque strings; a mismatch rejects with AGENT_PROVIDER_FAILED because the
      compiler owns no provider alias catalog

      rejection carries exactly one AdapterFailure code and discards every partial
      finding

      observe caller cancellation at evaluation entry, immediately before returning
      any preflight failure, and immediately before provider process creation.
      Cancellation observed at any of those points rejects with AGENT_CANCELLED,
      performs zero provider invocations, and takes precedence over another preflight
      failure

      successful settlement linearizes after valid provider completion, zero exit,
      every validation, and temporary-state cleanup, immediately before return;
      cancellation observed after process creation and at or before that point
      rejects with AGENT_CANCELLED, while cancellation first observed afterward does
      not replace the result

      preflight includes request, capability, budget, prompt rendering,
      maxInputChars, and the final pre-creation cancellation validation. Any
      preflight rejection performs zero provider invocations; a request that
      completes preflight performs exactly one provider invocation and never retries
    }

    AgentCommandTrace {
      contains sequence as a nonnegative safe integer equal to the entry's zero-based
      position, canonicalCommandFamily, providerOperationId, terminal status, and
      provider exit code when supplied

      providerOperationId is the provider-supplied non-empty string or null when the
      provider supplies no identity. When start and terminal events are distinct, an
      identifier is unique among open operations and correlates one terminal event to
      exactly one start; terminal-only events require no open-operation correlation

      contains one entry for every authorized settled operation in validated
      terminal-event order. Sequence is assigned when the terminal event is accepted;
      provider event gaps and rejected operations do not create trace gaps, and a
      successful no-command run contains an empty trace

      contains no raw arguments, environment values, command output, file content,
      credential, or secret; unavailable non-sensitive fields use null rather than a
      fabricated value

      terminal status is completed or failed; completed means the native operation
      emitted its successful terminal event and failed means it emitted a non-success
      terminal event

      completed and failed operations may appear in a successful result when the
      provider settles afterward; cancellation returns no result or command trace

      a missing or unrecognized terminal operation event rejects the adapter result
      with AGENT_EVENT_INVALID rather than creating a trace status
    }

    AdapterFailure {
      code is AGENT_CANCELLED, AGENT_REQUEST_INVALID, AGENT_BUDGET_INVALID,
      AGENT_TIMEOUT, AGENT_BUDGET_EXCEEDED, AGENT_CAPABILITY_UNENFORCEABLE,
      AGENT_PROVIDER_FAILED, AGENT_EVENT_INVALID, AGENT_SCHEMA_INVALID, or
      AGENT_USAGE_UNAVAILABLE

      capability mismatch maps to AGENT_CAPABILITY_UNENFORCEABLE; cancellation maps
      to AGENT_CANCELLED; timeout maps to AGENT_TIMEOUT; input-size or execution
      budget exhaustion maps to AGENT_BUDGET_EXCEEDED

      startup or nonzero exit maps to AGENT_PROVIDER_FAILED; malformed or non-settled
      events map to AGENT_EVENT_INVALID; missing or invalid final findings map to
      AGENT_SCHEMA_INVALID; missing or malformed mandatory usage maps to
      AGENT_USAGE_UNAVAILABLE

      when conditions overlap, choose AGENT_CANCELLED before AGENT_REQUEST_INVALID,
      then AGENT_BUDGET_INVALID, AGENT_TIMEOUT, AGENT_BUDGET_EXCEEDED,
      AGENT_CAPABILITY_UNENFORCEABLE, AGENT_EVENT_INVALID, AGENT_SCHEMA_INVALID,
      AGENT_USAGE_UNAVAILABLE, and AGENT_PROVIDER_FAILED in that precedence order

      preserve the selected primary failure when termination or temporary-state
      cleanup also fails; cleanup failure maps to AGENT_PROVIDER_FAILED only when no
      preceding failure exists
    }
  }
}
